{"id": "section-body-18264", "title": "Dentigerous cyst", "chapterId": "chapter-sixteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "ORAL AND MAXILLOFACIAL CONDITIONS", "Odontogenic and Non- Odontogenic Cysts", "Dentigerous cyst"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-18264", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Dentigerous cyst", "runs": [{"text": "Dentigerous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cyst"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1126"}}, {"id": "body-18265", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Dentigerous cysts, also called follicular cysts, are slow-growing benign and non-inflammatory odontogenic cysts that are thought to be developmental in origin.", "runs": [{"text": "Dentigerous cysts, also called follicular cysts, are slow-growing benign and non-inflammatory odontogenic cysts that are thought to be developmental in origin."}]}, {"id": "body-18267", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-18268", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Uninfected dentigerous cysts are painless and non - tender on palpation.", "runs": [{"text": "Uninfected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dentigerous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cysts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "painless"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tender"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "palpation."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1086"}}, {"id": "body-18269", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Larger cysts cause a marked, smooth, rounded expansion of the bone, which may be reduced to a thin layer of cortical plate.", "runs": [{"text": "Larger"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cysts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"tex